# Local env files must never reach a Vercel build.
#
# A .vercelignore replaces .gitignore for CLI uploads, so anything listed only in
# .gitignore still gets uploaded by `vercel deploy`. frontend/.env sets
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000 for local dev, and Vite inlines that at build time —
# a CLI deploy therefore shipped a production bundle hard-wired to localhost, with no
# backend URL in it at all. Git-triggered builds were never affected (the file is
# git-ignored and simply absent); this closes the same hole for CLI deploys.
.env
*.env
!*.env.example
.env.local
.env.*.local
